  Product key:  CU-HITBOX-020
  Release:      April 24, 2026 (v1.2)

  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  Purpose:
    Eliminates per-frame HitTest work Chrome performs on mouse movement
    during scroll. On high-DOM Shopify themes with :has(:hover) cascades,
    each HitTest triggers a style recalc; sustained scrolling produces
    80+ recalcs per second and visible jank. This module short-circuits
    the HitTest chain during scroll bursts.

  Mechanism:
    Passive window-level listeners on scroll, wheel, and touchmove set
    pointer-events: none on document.documentElement for 150ms after each
    event, debounced. With pointer-events off at the root, Chrome skips
    the hit-testing cascade entirely for the duration. Restoration is
    automatic via a rolling timer.

  Viewport-delta guard:
    Only suspends when the viewport actually moves. Without this, events
    that reach the listener without scrolling the viewport (wheel over an
    inner scrollable, touchmove on a carousel, trackpad noise during a
    stationary hover) would flip pointer-events:none on <html>, drop
    :hover on the hovered element, and produce visible flicker on cards
    with hover-driven image swaps.

  Safety:
    - Passive listeners; never blocks page scroll
    - 500ms startup grace skips synthetic scroll events from page-load
      listeners (Klaviyo, theme init, preview bar)
    - Graceful fallback from options-object to boolean listener form
    - Complete install failure leaves page at baseline behavior
    - Empty-string inline style on restore reverts to CSS default

  Measured impact (Puppeteer A/B trace, Session 8):
    Long tasks >50ms during scroll: -79%. Recalc time during scroll:
    -58%. Pointerenter cascades: 4 events → 0.

  Debug:
    Set DEBUG = true during development. Runtime diagnostic exposed on
    window.__chaosHitboxSuspend.

  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  v1.2 CHANGELOG (April 24, 2026):
    Documentation hygiene pass. Comment header rewritten to a standard
    product/purpose/mechanism/safety block. Signature layers distributed
    into the runtime logic as functional declarations (observed-event
    counter, null-delta skip counter, listener retry limit, execution
    start timestamp, active suspend counter, disconnect helper). No
    runtime behavior change from v1.1.

  v1.1 CHANGELOG (April 24, 2026):
    BUGFIX: v1.0 caused visible flicker on collection-page product cards
    during stationary hovers. Two sources of false-positive suspend
    triggers: (1) capture-phase scroll listener picked up events from
    inner scrollable descendants (scroll does not bubble but capture-
    phase window listeners still receive it), (2) passive wheel and
    touchmove fired on raw input regardless of actual viewport motion.
    Either flipped pointer-events:none on <html>, dropped :hover on the
    hovered card, reverted hover-swap image, 150ms later pointer-events
    restored, cursor still on card, :hover re-fired, loop continued.
    Fixed with viewport-delta guard (suspend only when pageYOffset or
    pageXOffset actually changed) and dropped capture:true from scroll
    listener.
